- crates/platform/workbench/src/workbench.rs (file drops, empty editor area),
  crates/platform/editor/src/editor.rs and element.rs (the caret during a drag)
  The handling of files dropped onto the main window follows the IntelliJ
  Platform Community (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community
  @ 27e7bdec710a61fe64b065c45585156355a1c686: the drop targets of
  platform/platform-impl/src/com/intellij/openapi/fileEditor/impl/
  EditorsSplitters.kt and EditorTabbedContainer.kt, the order of opening and
  the folders of .../openapi/editor/FileDropManager.kt, .../fileEditor/
  FileNavigatorImpl.kt and ProjectFileNavigatorImpl.kt, the caret that
  follows a drag in .../openapi/editor/impl/EditorImpl.java, the welcome
  screen's drop of .../wm/impl/welcomeScreen/ProjectsTabFactory.kt and
  .../ide/impl/ProjectUtil.kt (openOrImportFilesAsync), and the drop target
  of platform/lang-impl/src/com/intellij/ide/projectView/impl/
  ProjectViewDropTarget.java. The empty editor area follows .../fileEditor/
  impl/DefaultEditorEmptyTextProvider.kt (the list and order of the hints)
  and EditorEmptyTextPainter.java with platform/util/ui/src/com/intellij/
  util/ui/UIUtil.java (TextPainter: font size, line spacing, position), with
  the UI strings "Project View" and "Drop files here to open them" of
  platform/platform-api/resources/messages/IdeBundle.properties. Only
  behaviour, numbers and strings are used; reimplemented in Rust, no code is
  copied.

- crates/platform/editor/src/input.rs
  The structure of the platform input handler (UTF-16 conversions, marked
  text, replace-and-mark) follows GPUI's text input example (Apache-2.0),
  https://github.com/zed-industries/zed @ 69e2130 (the commit of the
  crates.io gpui 0.2.2 release), file crates/gpui/examples/input.rs.
  Changes: works on the rope buffer with multiple selections, undo groups and
  the editor's own layout for character bounds.

- crates/python/py-syntax/queries/highlights.scm
  Written for the tree-sitter-python grammar (MIT, (c) Max Brunsfeld and
  contributors, https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-python, used as
  the crates.io dependency tree-sitter-python 0.25.0); it uses the
  grammar's node names. The list of built-in names follows the Python
  documentation of built-in functions and exceptions. The grammar's own
  query is not copied.

